y and it's exhausting  focus instead on what you have to offer  this is the time for kindness and grace  and generosity are their senior citizens  that you know who can't get to a grocery  store or who could use a home-cooked  meal which are probably making more of  anyway these days and you must be  informed about this virus you cannot be  complacent you may be young and your  children may be even younger and while  children don't seem to be affected kids  can be carriers who would just a simple  hug or kiss to Grandma or anyone older  can pass something that may be harmless  to the child but lethal to the older  person pitch in it'll make you feel  better  we saw it just yesterday as the Giants  and private sectors stepped up with the  president Walmart Walgreens CVS and many  more to help us get through this even  though they know they're going to take a  big financial it like them we need to be  strong enough to know what we face and  strong enough to understand what we need  to do about it as the experts continue  their mission to fight this epidemic I  wonder how many of us will use this time  to examine our lives and assess what  really is important one minute we're  enjoying the bounties of life and then  like a thunderbolt  our lives are suddenly changed maybe  just maybe we are blessed with a time  for introspection my introspection is  informed by my belief in God take this  time to decide what's important to you
 

